 drinks, and sometimes activities.\\n*   **Be Flexible with Dates:** If your April dates are flexible by a few days, you might find better flight prices.\\n*   **Book in Advance (but not too early):** Aim to book flights and accommodation a few months out for the best balance of availability and price.\\n*   **Consider Less \\\"Trendy\\\" Destinations:** While popular spots are great, sometimes slightly less well-known but equally beautiful locations can offer better value.\\n*   **Factor in All Costs:** Remember to budget for airport transfers, travel insurance, potential visa fees (though unlikely for these destinations), and any activities or excursions you plan.\\n\\n**Potential Destinations to Research (once you can search):**\\n\\nThese are destinations that often have good flight availability from Toronto and can be done on a budget, especially in April.\\n\\n*   **Florida (USA):**\\n    *   **Why:** Relatively short flight from Toronto, many beach towns to choose from, and April is generally pleasant weather-wise before it gets too hot and humid. You can find a range of accommodation options from condos to hotels.\\n    *   **Areas to consider:** Gulf Coast (e.g., Clearwater, St. Pete Beach, Sarasota) for calmer waters, or the Atlantic Coast (e.g., Daytona Beach, Fort Lauderdale) for more activity.\\n    *   **Budgeting:** Look for deals on flights to Tampa (TPA), Fort Lauderdale (FLL), or Orlando (MCO) and then drive to your chosen beach.\\n*   **Mexico (Riviera Maya or Cancun Area):**\\n    *   **Why:** Many all-inclusive resorts can be very competitively priced, especially if you find a good package deal. April is typically outside of hurricane season and before the major summer heat.\\n    *   **Areas to consider:** Playa del Carmen, Cozumel (for snorkeling/diving), or even parts of Cancun.\\n    *   **Budgeting:** Focus on finding flight and resort packages. Be aware that some of the most luxurious resorts will push your budget.\\n*   **Dominican Republ